━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ FoldedNumber is Tuple

` The bits a constant number folds to, where it `folds`.

+ bits U64
+ folds Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ CallTyping is facet of Checker
    sees Comprehensions
    sees Markup
    sees Tables

────────────────────
_ held-type TypeId
    - type TypeId

` A type, or what it holds where it is an optional.
if types.is-optional(type) then types.optional-inner(type) else type

────────────────────
+ do infer-argument TypeId
    - expr SyntaxId
    - symbol Atom?

` An argument is typed outside any `catch` its call is written under: an error it raises
` leaves the function, and the catch holds only the errors of the call itself. One that names
` an event is its `Broadcastable` (see `use-event`).
if symbol
    = types.void-type
. caught = frame.surround
frame.surround = frame.surround.catch-depth = 0
. type = infer(expr, Want().adding(.want-argument))
frame.surround = caught
= type

────────────────────
_ do is-method Bool
    - owner ModuleId
    - decl DeclId

` Whether a function is a method of a type, which the value of a stored property cannot call:
` the object the method would run on is not yet made.
do match? program.modules[owner].decls[decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        if fn.owner == 0 || fn.is-static
            = false
        do match? program.modules[owner].decls[fn.owner]
            | .decl-class
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ eager-call-message String
    - name Atom
    - owner ModuleId
    - decl DeclId

|? eager-value()
    "A property's value is computed before the object exists, so it $called; declare the property without a value and assign it in a constructor's body"
??
    "A \"..\" initializer runs before the object exists, so it $called; compute the value from the constructor's parameters, or assign it in the constructor's body"

.. called = "cannot call \"${name.text}\", a method of ${method-owner(owner, decl)}"

────────────────────
_ eager-value Bool

|? reading.eager
    instances.is-initializer(instance)
??
    outer != null && outer.eager-value()

────────────────────
_ do method-owner String
    - owner ModuleId
    - decl DeclId

. decls = program.modules[owner].decls
do match? decls[decl]
    | .decl-function(fn)
        do match? decls[fn.owner]
            | .decl-class(class)
                = class.name.text
= ""

────────────────────
_ do settle-kept-arguments
    - mark Size
    - result TypeId

` Declines each event read in a function written in a markup element's body that a call since
` `mark` was given and no converter refused (`misused-endpoint`), which has no shape here.
while kept-arguments.length > mark
    . kept = kept-arguments.pop()
    if kept != 0 && result != invalid-type
        decline(kept)

────────────────────
+ do infer-argument-value TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - row ASTArgument

` An argument written where a value is wanted, as a line of a markup element's body, as the
` reference compiles one: one with a name is the tuple of its name and its value, and one with a
` bullet `•?` too is that tuple where the value tests as true, as a condition does, and nothing
` where it does not; one with no name is its value.
. value = infer(row.expr)
if value == invalid-type || value == no-type || !row.name
    = value
. mark = scratch.types.mark
. names-mark = scratch.names.mark
scratch.names.push(types.index-atom(0))
scratch.types.push(types.string-type)
scratch.names.push(types.index-atom(1))
scratch.types.push(value)
. pair = types.intern-tuple(mark, names-mark)
if !row.is-optional
    = pair
note-truthiness(id, row.expr, value)
= types.optional-around(pair)

────────────────────
+ do infer-call Found
    - id SyntaxId
    - callable SyntaxId
    - params RowRange'SyntaxId
    - args RowRange'SyntaxId
    - curried Bool
    - attributes SyntaxId = 0
    - class TypeId = no-type
    - want Want = Want()
    - slots ImmutableArray'Atom'ArenaBacking = ImmutableArray'Atom'ArenaBacking()
    - builders ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking = ImmutableArray'TypeId'ArenaBacking()
    - context U32 = U32.max

` A call written with its arguments. A markup element gives, after them, the value of each
` of the `attributes` its body writes for the `class` it makes, as an argument named as the
` property and marked as one, and its constructor the `slots` its body fills, each with the type
` of its builder (`builders`), and the `context` of the styles it sees. The arguments of a call of a name nothing declares are typed as
` the reference types them before it finds no function (`names-nothing`).
. owner = if want.asks(.want-owner) then held-type(want.type) else no-type
. params-start = scratch.types.mark
. param-count = 0
. unresolved = false
for param in tree.children[params]
    . written = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, param, frame.env)
    unresolved = unresolved || written == invalid-type
    scratch.types.push(written)
    param-count += 1
. listing = tree.listed-bullets(id)
=? Found(infer-listed-bullets(id, callable, listing)) if listing != 0
if args.count == 1
    do match? tree.nodes[callable]
        | .node-type-arguments
            . only = tree.children[args.start]
            expect-bullets(only, types.evaluate-type(module, tree, callable, frame.env))
. shapes-start = scratch.call-arguments.mark
. types-start = scratch.types.mark
. syntax-start = scratch.syntax.mark
. object = if attributes != 0 then CalledObject() else type-called-object(callable, args.count)
. outer-unknown = argument-typing
. kept-mark = kept-arguments.length
argument-typing = argument-typing.unknown-callee = attributes == 0 && names-nothing(callable, args)
argument-typing = argument-typing.keeps = true
for arg in tree.children[args]
    do match tree.nodes[arg]
        | .node-argument(argument)
            scratch.types.push(infer-argument(argument.expr, tree.argument-symbol(argument.expr)))
            scratch.call-arguments.push
                - argument-shape(argument.name, argument.is-optional, argument.expr)
            scratch.syntax.push(arg)
        ??
            scratch.types.push(infer-argument(arg, tree.argument-symbol(arg)))
            scratch.call-arguments.push(argument-shape(null, false, arg))
            scratch.syntax.push(arg)
argument-typing = outer-unknown
. given = attributes == 0 || push-attributes(attributes, class)
. missing = given && unresolved && report-missing-params(params)
. params = scratch.types.span(params-start, param-count)
. arguments = arguments-since(shapes-start, types-start, syntax-start, params, curried, 0, slots, builders, context)
called-object = object
. result = if given && !missing then infer-callable(id, callable, arguments, owner) else Found(invalid-type)
settle-kept-arguments(kept-mark, result.type)
called-object = CalledObject()
scratch.syntax.rewind(syntax-start)
scratch.types.rewind(params-start)
scratch.call-arguments.rewind(shapes-start)
=? Found(invalid-type) if result.type != invalid-type && tracks-method(id, callable)
= result

────────────────────
_ do tracks-method Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - callable SyntaxId

` Reports a method called with "#" before its name, as in `c.#size()`, which tracks nothing, as
` only a stored property is tracked, and says whether it did.
. name Atom? = null
do match? tree.nodes[callable]
    | .node-get-expression(get)
        name = get.name if get.is-tracked
    | .node-identifier(ident)
        name = ident.name if ident.is-tracked
if !name
    = false
. fact = facts.first-call(instance, id)
while fact != no-fact
    if facts.calls[fact].form == .call-method
        . text = "\"${name.text}\" is a method, so \"#\" before it tracks nothing; track the properties it reads instead"
        frame.diagnose(callable, .stated, program.store-atom(text))
        = true
    fact = facts.calls[fact].next
= false

────────────────────
_ do report-missing-params Bool
    - params RowRange'SyntaxId

` Reports the first type written after a call's name that names nothing, as the reference does
` once it has typed the arguments. Says whether one was reported.
for param in tree.children[params]
    if report-missing-type(param, frame.env)
        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ do type-called-object CalledObject
    - callable SyntaxId
    - count Size

` Types the object of a method a call names, which the reference evaluates before the call's
` arguments, so that what the flow knows of it is what it knew before them. The call is
` settled with it once its arguments are typed (`infer-callable`). A type a static method is
` called on is no value, and nothing is typed of it here.
do match? tree.nodes[callable]
    | .node-get-expression(get)
        if static-owner(get.object) != no-type
            = CalledObject()
        . writes = get.name.text == "<-write" && count == 1
        . rekeys = get.name.text == "rekey" && count == 1
        . asks-event = (writes || rekeys || (get.name.text == "release" && count == 0)) && !get.is-optional
        . want = Want().adding(.want-receiver)
        . receiver = infer-found(get.object, if asks-event then want.adding(.want-event) else want)
        = CalledObject(get.object, receiver.type, receiver.link, found-event-of(receiver))
= CalledObject()

────────────────────
+ do infer-callable Found
    - id SyntaxId
    - callable SyntaxId
    - arguments Arguments
    - owner TypeId = no-type

for type in arguments.types
    if type == invalid-type
        = Found(invalid-type)
do match? tree.nodes[callable]
    | .node-c-identifier(row)
        = Found(calls.c-call(id, row.name, arguments))
    | .node-type-identifier(row)
        . is-this = types.this-atom && row.name == types.this-atom
        if is-this || bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, callable).kind != .resolve-type
            = Found(construct-type(id, callable, arguments))
    | .node-type-arguments
        if bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, callable).kind != .resolve-type
            = Found(construct-type(id, callable, arguments))
    | .node-type-associated
        = Found(construct-type(id, callable, arguments))
    | .node-symbol(row)
        if owner != no-type
            = Found(calls.static-call(id, owner, row.name, arguments))
        . anonymous = anonymous-symbol(callable, row.name)
        if anonymous == invalid-type
            = Found(invalid-type)
        if anonymous != no-type
            = Found(calls.static-call(id, anonymous, row.name, arguments))
        if calls.ambiguous-case(callable, row.name)
            = Found(invalid-type)
        . named = symbol-class(types, module, row.name)
        if named == invalid-type
            frame.diagnose
                - id
                - .stated
                - program.store-atom("Unable to resolve symbol .${row.name.text}")
            = Found(invalid-type)
        = Found(calls.static-call(id, named, row.name, arguments))
    | .node-get-expression(get)
        . owner = static-owner(get.object)
        if owner != no-type
            = Found(call-static(id, get.object, owner, get.name, arguments))
        . typed = called-object
        called-object = CalledObject()
        if typed.object != get.object
            typed = type-called-object(callable, arguments.types.length)
        . receiver = typed.type
        if typed.event
            . event = typed.event
            . writes = get.name.text == "<-write" && arguments.types.length == 1
            . rekeys = get.name.text == "rekey" && arguments.types.length == 1
            if writes
                . published = publish-event(id, get.object, event, arguments)
                if published != invalid-type && optional-chained(get.object)
                    = Found(types.optional-of(published))
                = Found(published)
            = Found(readdress-event(id, get.object, event, arguments, rekeys))
        . own = typed.link
        if receiver == invalid-type
            = Found(invalid-type)
        if is-super-syntax(get.object) && receiver != frame.self-type
            conversions.convert(id, id, frame.self-type, receiver, .reason-receiver)
        . source = projected-from(get.object, receiver)
        if source != no-type && !calls.has-method(receiver, get.name, arguments)
            receiver = source
        . form = if get.is-optional then note-chain(id, callable, receiver) else plain-form
            .. plain-form = ChainForm.chain-plain
        if form == .chain-absent || absent-after(get.object, receiver)
            = Found(types.null-type)
        . optional = form == .chain-tested
        . held = link-receiver(get.object, receiver, own, optional)
        if !optional && !(optional-chained(get.object) && types.is-optional(receiver))
            if calls-property(get.object, receiver, get.name, arguments)
                . value = read-property(callable, get.object, receiver, get.name).type
                if value == invalid-type
                    = Found(value)
                facts.set-node-type(instance, callable, value)
                = Found(call-value(id, callable, value, arguments))
            . answered = calls.method-call(id, get.object, receiver, get.name, arguments, true, row-capture-of(get.object))
            if answered != invalid-type && types.intrinsic-of(receiver) == .table
                . op = table-member(get.name.text)
                if op != TableOp.table-row && op != TableOp.table-mark && not-capacity
                    plan-table(id, op)
                .. not-capacity = op != TableOp.table-capacity
            if answered != invalid-type
                plan-builder(id, receiver, get.name.text, arguments.types.length)
            if answered == types.void-type && get.name.text == "<-write"
                = Found(receiver)
            = Found(answered)
        if optional
            facts.unwrapped.append(UnwrappedFact(instance, get.object, held))
        . result = calls.method-call(id, get.object, held, get.name, arguments, true)
        if result == invalid-type || types.is-optional(result)
            = Found(result).linking(result)
        = Found(types.optional-of(result)).linking(result)
if is-super-syntax(callable) || tree.names-super(callable)
    = Found(super-call(id, callable, arguments))
. resolution = bindings.resolution-of(frame.binding, callable)
do match resolution.kind
    |= .resolve-function
        . name = tree.identifier-name(callable)
        if !name
            decline(id)
            = Found(invalid-type)
        if in-eager() && is-method(resolution.module, resolution.decl)
            frame.diagnose
                - id
                - .stated
                - program.store-atom(eager-call-message(name, resolution.module, resolution.decl))
            = Found(invalid-type)
        . answered = calls.function-call(id, name, arguments)
        if answered != invalid-type && is-method(resolution.module, resolution.decl)
            plan-builder(id, frame.self-type, name.text, arguments.types.length)
        = Found(answered)
    |= .resolve-type
        . called = tree.identifier-name(callable)
        if called && types.this-atom && called == types.this-atom
            = Found(construct-type(id, callable, arguments))
        if types.const-array-decl.refers-to(resolution.module, resolution.decl)
            = Found(construct-type(id, callable, arguments))
        if resolution.module == types.table-module && !is-row-table(callable, arguments)
            = Found(invalid-type)
        . (class-module, class-decl) = taking-class(callable, resolution.module, resolution.decl)
        = Found(calls.construction(id, callable, class-module, class-decl, arguments))
    |= .resolve-slot
        if bindings.slots[resolution.slot].getter != 0
            decline(callable)
            = Found(invalid-type)
        if precedes-declaration(resolution.slot)
            frame.diagnose(id, .function-not-found, tree.identifier-name(callable))
            = Found(invalid-type)
        if wavers(resolution.slot)
            decline(id)
            = Found(invalid-type)
        . called = read-slot(resolution.slot, id)
        . declared = slot-known(resolution.slot)
        if declared != called && types.is-optional(declared) && unwraps-called
            facts.set-plan(instance, callable, .plan-callee)
        .. unwraps-called = types.optional-inner(declared) == called
        = Found(call-value(id, callable, called, arguments))
    |= .resolve-member
        . name = tree.identifier-name(callable)
        if !name
            decline(id)
            = Found(invalid-type)
        . held = read-member(callable, name).type
        . key = member-key(resolution.decl)
        . narrowed = if frame.members-narrowed then frame.narrowed-member(key) else no-type
        . declared = if narrowed != no-type then key-declared(key) else no-type
        . unwraps = optional-declared && types.optional-inner(declared) == held
            .. optional-declared = declared != no-type && types.is-optional(declared)
        if held != invalid-type && held == narrowed && (callable-held || unwraps)
            facts.set-plan(instance, callable, .plan-callee)
        .. callable-held = function-row(types, held) != no-type
        = Found(call-value(id, callable, held, arguments))
    |= .resolve-global
        . held = infer-node(callable, Want())
        if held == invalid-type
            = Found(held)
        = Found(call-value(id, callable, held, arguments))
    |= .resolve-unresolved
        . name = tree.identifier-name(callable)
        if !name
            = Found(invalid-type)
        . bound = types.env-lookup(frame.env, name)
        if bound
            = Found(calls.construction-on(id, bound, arguments, true, callable))
        = Found(calls.function-call(id, name, arguments))
    ??
        . target = infer(callable)
        if target == invalid-type
            = Found(target)
        . kind = types.intrinsic-of(target)
        if kind == .closure || kind == .binding || function-row(types, target) != no-type
            = Found(calls.slot-call(id, target, arguments))
        = Found(calls.method-call(id, callable, target, types.call-atom!, arguments))

────────────────────
_ calls-property Bool
    - object SyntaxId
    - receiver TypeId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments

` Whether a call written as a method call reads a property and calls what it holds, as the
` reference does where the receiver has no method of the name but a property or a getter of
` it. A union, a type given as a value, and `super` are called only for their methods.
|? is-super-syntax(object)
    false
|? kind == .union || kind == .type-info || calls.has-method(receiver, name, arguments)
    false
??
    property-named(receiver, name) != null || calls.has-getter(receiver, name)

.. kind = types.intrinsic-of(receiver)

────────────────────
_ do super-call TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callable SyntaxId
    - arguments Arguments

` `super(...)` runs the base class's constructor: only in a constructor, only as its first
` statement, and only when there is a base.
. self = frame.self-type
. based = self != no-type && self != invalid-type && types.base-of(self) != null
. message = ""
if !based
    message = "super requires a base type"
else if !is-constructor-kind(frame.declaration.kind)
    message = "super constructor call is only allowed in constructors"
else if body-statements().count == 0 || tree.children[body-statements().start] != id
    message = "super constructor call must be first"
if message.length != 0
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
= calls.construction-on(id, super-type(), arguments, false, callable)

────────────────────
_ do call-value TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callable SyntaxId
    - target TypeId
    - arguments Arguments

` A call of what a name holds: a value of a function type is called, and a value of any
` other type is given to the function its type declares for a call of it.
if target == invalid-type || types.completions[target].intrinsic == .closure
    = calls.slot-call(id, target, arguments)
types.complete(target)
. kind = types.completions[target].intrinsic
if kind != .binding && function-row(types, target) == no-type
    = calls.method-call(id, callable, target, types.call-atom!, arguments)
= calls.slot-call(id, target, arguments)

────────────────────
_ type-head SyntaxId
    - id SyntaxId

` The name a type is written with, under the arguments it is given.
match tree.nodes[id]
    | .node-type-arguments(row)
        type-head(row.base)
    ??
        id

────────────────────
_ do construct-type TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - callable SyntaxId
    - arguments Arguments

if names-const-array(callable)
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom("ConstArray requires one item type"))
    = invalid-type
types.clear-fault()
. receiver = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, callable, frame.env)
if receiver == invalid-type
    if report-circular() || report-fault(callable)
        = invalid-type
    . head = type-head(callable)
    if names-nothing(head)
        frame.diagnose(head, .constructor-not-found)
    else
        decline(id)
    = invalid-type
if is-const-array(receiver)
    . item = cpointer-item(receiver)
    . items [ConstItem]
    . folds = true
    for position in 0 .. < arguments.types.length
        . site = arguments.syntax[position]
        . shape = arguments.shapes[position]
        if shape.name || shape.is-property
            frame.diagnose(site, .stated, program.store-atom("Illegal ConstArray item"))
            = invalid-type
        conversions.convert(site, site, arguments.types[position], item, .reason-argument)
        if is-computed(site)
            . message = program.store-atom("ConstArray item must be constant")
            frame.diagnose(site, .stated, message)
            = invalid-type
        . folded = fold-const-item(site, item)
        if folded
            items += folded
        else
            folds = false
    if folds
        facts.note-const-array(instance, id, receiver, items)
    = receiver
. by-name = true
do match? tree.nodes[callable]
    | .node-type-identifier(row)
        if types.this-atom && row.name == types.this-atom
            by-name = false
            if frame.self-type != no-type
                receiver = frame.self-type
if !check-table-row(receiver, arguments)
    = invalid-type
= calls.construction-on
    - id
    - receiver
    - arguments
    - by-name
    - if tree.nodes[id] is .node-markup then id else callable

────────────────────
_ do fold-const-item ConstItem?
    - site SyntaxId
    - item TypeId

` An item of a ConstArray as TypeScript lays it down: a string literal, or a number folded
` to its bits and cut to the width of an integer item. Nothing for any other.
do match? tree.nodes[site]
    | .node-argument(row)
        = fold-const-item(row.expr, item)
    | .node-string-syntax
        if item == types.string-type
            = ConstItem(0, site)
        = null
. kind = types.completions[item].intrinsic
if !is-integer-kind(kind)
    = null
. folded = fold-number(site)
if !folded.folds
    = null
= ConstItem(cut-bits(folded.bits, item), 0)

────────────────────
_ do fold-number FoldedNumber
    - site SyntaxId

` The integer a literal number is, negated or cast to an integer type, as its bits.
do match? tree.nodes[site]
    | .node-argument(row)
        = fold-number(row.expr)
    | .node-integer-syntax(row)
        . literal = parse-integer-literal(row.value)
        if literal.overflow
            = FoldedNumber(0, false)
        = FoldedNumber(if literal.negative then 0 - literal.value else literal.value, true)
    | .node-unary-expression(row)
        if row.op == .negative-op
            . inner = fold-number(row.operand)
            = FoldedNumber(0 - inner.bits, inner.folds)
    | .node-cast-expression(row)
        . inner = fold-number(row.lhs)
        . target = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, row.rhs, frame.env)
        if inner.folds && target != invalid-type && integer-target
            = FoldedNumber(cut-bits(inner.bits, target), true)
        .. integer-target = is-integer-kind(types.completions[target].intrinsic)
= FoldedNumber(0, false)

────────────────────
_ cut-bits U64
    - bits U64
    - type TypeId

` Bits cut to the width of an integer type and extended by its sign.
|? width >= 64 || width == 0
    bits
??
    if negative then kept /or/ (mask /xor/ U64.max) else kept

.. row = types.completions[type]
.. width = row.bit-size as U64
.. mask = (1u64 /lshift/ width) - 1
.. kept = bits /and/ mask
.. negative = row.is-signed && (kept /rshift/ (width - 1)) != 0

────────────────────
_ do taking-class (ModuleId, DeclId)
    - callable SyntaxId
    - named-module ModuleId
    - named DeclId

` The class a callable written with type arguments makes: the one its name resolves to, or where
` that takes fewer type arguments than are written, the first class of the name this module sees
` that takes as many or more, as the reference passes over one that takes fewer.
do match? tree.nodes[callable]
    | .node-type-arguments(row)
        . given Size = row.args.count
        . taken Size = types.class-type-args(named-module, named).count
        . name = types.type-syntax-name(tree, row.base)
        if taken < given && name
            for candidate in program.lookup(module, name)
                do match? program.modules[candidate.module].decls[candidate.decl]
                    | .decl-class
                        . held Size = types.class-type-args(candidate.module, candidate.decl).count
                        if held >= given
                            = (candidate.module, candidate.decl)
= (named-module, named)

────────────────────
_ do names-const-array Bool
    - callable SyntaxId

` Whether a callable names ConstArray without the type of its items.
do match? tree.nodes[callable]
    | .node-type-identifier(row)
        if row.name != types.const-array-atom!
            = false
        . named = types.type-named(module, row.name, frame.env)
        = named != invalid-type && is-const-array(named)
= false

────────────────────
_ do is-computed Bool
    - site SyntaxId

` Whether an item is the result of a call, which no constant array can hold.
do match? tree.nodes[site]
    | .node-argument(row)
        = is-computed(row.expr)
    | .node-call-expression(row)
        do match? tree.nodes[row.callable]
            | .node-identifier
                = true
            | .node-get-expression
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do call-static TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - object SyntaxId
    - owner TypeId
    - name Atom
    - arguments Arguments

` A call on a type. It is a call of a static method when the type is a type parameter, an
` interface, or a type that declares a static method of the name: a type parameter answers
` only what its constraints declare, an interface answers nothing itself, and a static method
` that takes no such arguments is reported as one.
. dependent = dependent-name(object)
. interface = types.intrinsic-of(owner) == .interface
if !dependent && !interface && !declares-static(owner, name)
    . answered = calls.static-call(id, owner, name, arguments)
    note-type-value(id, object)
    = answered
if !dependent && interface
    . message = "Static methods cannot be called on an interface type"
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
if dependent && !requires-static(dependent, name)
    . shown = dependent.text
    . message = "Static method ${name.text} is not declared by constraints on $shown"
    frame.diagnose(id, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = invalid-type
. diagnosed = facts.diagnostics.length
. result = calls.static-call(id, owner, name, arguments)
if result == invalid-type
    . message = program.store-atom("Static function not found")
    facts.restate(diagnosed, instance, id, .function-not-found, .stated, message)
= result

────────────────────
_ do note-type-value
    - id SyntaxId
    - object SyntaxId

` A type that no static method answers for is called as the value describing it, and the
` type's name is that value.
. fact = facts.first-call(instance, id)
if fact == no-fact || facts.calls[fact].callee == no-instance
    =
. receiver = instances.rows[facts.calls[fact].callee].self-type
if receiver != no-type && types.intrinsic-of(receiver) == .type-info
    facts.set-node-type(instance, object, receiver)

────────────────────
_ do dependent-name Atom?
    - object SyntaxId

` The type parameter a type's name stands for, when it names one.
do match? tree.nodes[object]
    | .node-type-identifier(row)
        . this-name = types.this-atom
        if this-name && this-name == row.name
            = null
        if types.env-lookup(frame.env, row.name)
            = row.name
= null

────────────────────
_ do requires-static Bool
    - param Atom
    - name Atom

` Whether a constraint on a type parameter, of the function or converter or of the type it
` belongs to, declares a static method of the name.
. decls = program.modules[module].decls
. decl = frame.decl
while decl != 0
    . constraints = RowRange'SyntaxId()
    . next = 0u32
    do match? decls[decl]
        | .decl-function(fn)
            constraints = fn.param-constraints
            next = fn.owner
        | .decl-converter(converter)
            constraints = converter.param-constraints
            next = converter.owner
        | .decl-fromverter(fromverter)
            next = fromverter.owner
        | .decl-class(class)
            constraints = class.param-constraints
    for constraint in tree.children[constraints]
        do match? tree.nodes[constraint]
            | .node-param-constraint(row)
                . constrained = types.type-syntax-name(tree, row.left)
                if constrained && constrained == param
                    . bound = types.evaluate-type(module, tree, row.right, frame.env)
                    if bound != invalid-type && declares-static(bound, name)
                        = true
    decl = next
= false

────────────────────
_ do declares-static Bool
    - type TypeId
    - name Atom

` Whether a type, a base of it, or an interface it implements declares a static method.
types.complete(type)
do match? types.rows[type]
    | .type-class(row)
        . owner = program.modules[row.module]
        do match? owner.decls[row.decl]
            | .decl-class(class)
                for member in owner.members-named(class.members, name)
                    do match? owner.decls[member]
                        | .decl-function(fn)
                            if fn.is-static && fn.name && fn.name == name
                                = true
for interface in types.interfaces-of(type)
    if declares-static(interface, name)
        = true
. base = types.base-of(type)
if base
    = declares-static(base, name)
= false

────────────────────
+ do call-override TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - op Operator
    - left SyntaxId
    - lhs TypeId
    - right SyntaxId
    - rhs TypeId
    - exchanged Bool

` Calls the operator one operand declares for the other, which for equality may be either
` operand, and gives no type when neither declares it. `exchanged` says the operands arrive
` in the reverse of their order in the source, so the call notes when its receiver is the
` operator's right operand.
. token = program.store-atom("$op")
if calls.has-operator(lhs, token, rhs)
    . result = calls.operator-call(id, lhs, token, right, rhs)
    if exchanged && result != invalid-type
        facts.mark-swapped(instance, id)
    = result
. either = op == .equals-op || op == .not-equals-op
if either && calls.has-operator(rhs, token, lhs)
    . result = calls.operator-call(id, rhs, token, left, lhs)
    if !exchanged && result != invalid-type
        facts.mark-swapped(instance, id)
    = result
= no-type
